    "notes": "Individual Gate of Felicity Q6041550 and OSM way32396111/native35184404484943. Its approximately97x22m notched connected gate-and-wing footprint fixes shape and placement. The projecting canopy lies on the Second Courtyard side southwest. Internal+X follows the front wall east-southeast; internal+Z faces Second Courtyard south-southwest, internal-Z the Third Courtyard north-northeast. Native world+X east/+Z south at heading0. The Audience Chamber is separately mapped immediately behind and remains independent. Existing standard PMTiles/Mapzen terrain retained. Native front-path control internal[3.8,23] sets Y0; rear control[3.8,-12] defines the modest through-passage cross slope. Connected wings follow nine front-ground samples along their length, preserving original terrain outside the tightly occupied mapped parent. Roof/floor subdivisions follow those controls; columns remain upright. This is an explicit approximate adaptation to the host terrain, whose eastern wing drops several metres. No broad courtyard slab, terrain flattening, independent-building replacement or water cutout. Original native terrain, footprint ownership, front-facing entry and approximate exterior contact were visually inspected2026-10-21 and accepted. The independent Audience Chamber procedural shell meets the rear boundary and obscures a distant rear view; the authored rear portico remains intact and is inspected from inside its own footprint. Exact historical wing levels and host terrain accuracy remain approximate. Only named Gate of Felicity OSM way32396111/native parent35184404484943 replaced. All258 independent resident records of259 and572 wider records of573 retained. Nine actual overlapping PMTiles13/14/15 cases pass. Original161x161/6m samples, paths and3400906.0006393427square metres native water unchanged. The notched occupied floor seals only its parent terrain opening; the gate route remains clear. Failure keeps259 originals; all four LOD unloads restore terrain/water/zero live geometry. Native overall/front contact and signed facing accepted. Approximate internal facade-bearing uncertainty10degrees. Existing standard ground controls produce a substantial eastern-wing descent; the floor/roof follow this host ground, not a surveyed historic leveling plan. An independent native Audience Chamber shell meets the rear boundary, so the rear portico is reviewed from inside its own footprint. Flat control fixtures do not certify native contact; exact thresholds, floor levels and accessible routes are not certified."
