    "notes": "Two ordinary photographs actually viewed: Second Courtyard front2023 and Third Courtyard rear2016. Standard PMTiles supplies the particular notched connected gate-and-wing footprint, paths and independent Audience Chamber boundary. Picture-led working wing eaves about6m above local occupied floor, central octagonal drum to8.15m, faceted lead dome to11.5m and main finial to12.95m; canopy shafts to5.15m and wing/rear shafts to3.65m. Portal clear width3.1m, spring2.7m/rise0.75m above local grade. These heights, eave curves, arch profiles, shaft spacing, gold finial shapes and paneled-door proportions are approximate visualization geometry, not surveyed dimensions, exact current condition or engineering/access certification. Recognition comes from the dome, deep columned canopy, real route and side arcades; fine painted ceiling art is excluded. Neutral original geometric accents replace ceiling scenes/inscriptions. Topkapi Palace is an18-member collection; this individual gate does not complete the palace."
